  <p>
    <strong>Key Takeaway:</strong> Neutron stars are cosmic laboratories where gravity creates the most extreme
    stable conditions in the universe. Their incredible density, powerful magnetic fields, rapid rotation, and
    strong gravity enable tests of physics impossible any other way. From their interiors to their collisions,
    neutron stars continue to reveal secrets about matter, gravity, and the fundamental laws of nature.
  </p>
